    <node id="PROVIDER">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">PROVIDER is a healthcare professional whose role encompasses the investigation of symptoms, the ordering or recommendation of imaging studies, and the scheduling of procedures such as standard biopsies. In addition, PROVIDER is a healthcare professional who provides cancer care and places trust in the NCCN Guidelines to inform clinical decision-making. Together, these descriptions depict PROVIDER as an active, guideline-informed clinician involved in the diagnostic and procedural aspects of cancer management.
Relationships:
  - Source: PROVIDER
  - Target: CARE TEAM
  - Description: The provider is part of the care team and schedules or recommends needed procedures.
  - Source: PROVIDER
  - Target: BIOPSY
  - Description: The provider will schedule a standard biopsy when a resection is not possible.
  - Source: PROVIDER
  - Target: IMAGING
  - Description: If symptoms are present, the provider may want a closer look, leading to imaging.
  - Source: PROVIDER
  - Target: NEUROSURGEON
  - Description: A provider may schedule a standard biopsy, and the neurosurgeon performs the surgical procedure.
  - Source: PROVIDER
  - Target: NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS
  - Description: The guidelines are trusted by providers to explain cancer care recommendations</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
