    <node id="PHYSICIAN">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A physician is a healthcare professional and a member of the care team. They may receive portal messages as part of patient communication, but they may not see these messages immediately. Therefore, urgent concerns should not be sent via portal message and should instead be called directly to triage.
Relationships:
  - Source: HEALTH CARE PROVIDER
  - Target: PHYSICIAN
  - Description: A physician is a type of health care provider
  - Source: CARE TEAM
  - Target: PHYSICIAN
  - Description: The physician is a member of the care team. Physicians, as individual practitioners, belong to the broader care team, which includes multiple roles working collaboratively. Thus, the relationship is clear: physicians are one component of the care team.
  - Source: MYCHART
  - Target: PHYSICIAN
  - Description: MyChart (the patient portal) messages are not immediately seen by a physician. Because of this, any urgent concerns should not be sent through MyChart or portal messaging; instead, they should be called directly to triage. Physicians do not monitor MyChart messages in real time, so portal messaging is not appropriate for time-sensitive or urgent medical issues.
  - Source: PRIMARY CARE PHYSICIAN (PCP)
  - Target: PHYSICIAN
  - Description: A primary care physician is a physician

---</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
