    <node id="MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST">
      <data key="d3">4</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST is a physician who specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of cancer through the use of systemic drug therapy. As a key member of the cancer care team, a medical oncologist treats cancer using medications that may be administered by mouth, injection, or intravenously. This specialist is specifically trained to prescribe and manage cancer-treatment drugs, including chemotherapy, and plays a central role in coordinating a patient's overall cancer treatment plan.
Relationships:
  - Source: MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST
  - Target: PHARMACIST
  - Description: Pharmacists work with medical oncologists by preparing and dispensing the cancer drugs they prescribe
  - Source: MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST
  - Target: CARE TEAM
  - Description: The CARE TEAM may include a MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST, and in some cases, care teams may include multiple medical oncologists. A medical oncologist is therefore a possible member of the care team, contributing specialized expertise in cancer treatment as part of the broader multidisciplinary group.
  - Source: MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST
  - Target: CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Medical oncologists prescribe chemotherapy and other cancer-treatment drugs
  - Source: MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST
  - Target: SYSTEMIC THERAPY
  - Description: A medical oncologist treats cancer using systemic drug therapy.</data>
