    <node id="CIRRHOSIS">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Cirrhosis is a chronic liver disease characterized by scarring of the liver. It is recognized as a known and major risk factor for liver cancer, and as such, it serves as an important indication for liver cancer screening. Risk assessments for liver cancer often compare individuals with cirrhosis to those without the condition, highlighting the elevated risk associated with the disease.
Relationships:
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: LIVER CANCER
  - Description: Cirrhosis is a major risk factor for the development of liver cancer. It is formally listed as a risk factor for liver cancer, and clinical comparisons are often made between individuals who have cirrhosis and those who do not, highlighting the elevated risk associated with the condition. In this context, cirrhosis and liver cancer are closely linked, with cirrhosis representing a significant predisposing condition for the onset of liver cancer.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: LIVER CANCER SCREENING
  - Description: People with cirrhosis should be enrolled in a liver cancer screening program.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: HEPATITIS B
  - Description: Hepatitis B virus or infection can cause cirrhosis.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: HEPATITIS C
  - Description: Hepatitis C virus or infection can cause cirrhosis.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: HEPATITIS
  - Description: Hepatitis can cause cirrhosis.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: NON-ALCOHOLIC FATTY LIVER DISEASE (NAFLD)
  - Description: NAFLD may lead to cirrhosis.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: CHRONIC HEPATITIS
  - Description: Chronic hepatitis can lead to cirrhosis.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: LIVER DISEASE
  - Description: Cirrhosis is a type of chronic liver disease.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: ALCOHOL USE
  - Description: Alcohol use can cause cirrhosis.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: GENETIC HEMOCHROMATOSIS
  - Description: Genetic hemochromatosis is listed as a cause of cirrhosis.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: STAGE 4 PRIMARY BILIARY CHOLANGITIS
  - Description: Stage 4 primary biliary cholangitis is listed as a cause of cirrhosis.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: ALPHA-1-ANTITRYPSIN DEFICIENCY
  - Description: Alpha-1-antitrypsin deficiency is listed as a cause of cirrhosis.</data>
