    <node id="PROSTATE CANCER">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Prostate cancer is a disease process in which cells in the prostate gland grow out of control. The condition is categorized into early-stage (localized) and advanced-stage (regional/metastatic) forms, reflecting the extent of the disease within or beyond the prostate. As the disease being evaluated, prostate cancer is assessed using several clinical tools: PSA density, Gleason score, and Grade Group, which together help estimate the likelihood of the disease and its aggressiveness. Additionally, the broader text covering prostate cancer addresses its risk factors, stages, screening, and treatment options, providing a comprehensive overview of the disease from diagnosis to management.
Relationships: (No relationships were provided in the data for this entity.)</data>
