    <node id="PROGNOSIS">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">PROGNOSIS is a medical term referring to the likely course and outcome of a disease, essentially predicting how a patient’s illness will turn out. In the context of cancer, prognosis specifically denotes the expected progression and final result of the disease, including the likelihood of recovery, recurrence, or survival. For prostate cancer, prognosis is based on risk group classification and is used to guide treatment options. Genetic and biomarker tests also help determine prognosis in cancer by providing molecular information that refines predictions about disease behavior. Overall, prognosis integrates clinical factors and test results to offer a forecast of disease trajectory, informing both patients and clinicians in decision-making.
Relationships:
  - Source: PROGNOSIS
  - Target: RECURRENCE
  - Description: Prognosis includes the likelihood of recurrence.
  - Source: PROGNOSIS
  - Target: PROSTATE CANCER
  - Description: For prostate cancer, prognosis is based on risk group classification and guides treatment options.
  - Source: PROGNOSIS
  - Target: GENETIC TESTS
  - Description: Genetic tests help determine prognosis.
  - Source: PROGNOSIS
  - Target: BIOMARKER TEST
  - Description: Biomarker tests help determine prognosis.</data>
