    <node id="SURVIVORSHIP">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Survivorship is the post-treatment phase of cancer care dedicated to supporting individuals after active treatment has ended. This phase focuses on addressing and managing long-term side effects that may persist or emerge following treatment, while also emphasizing the adoption and maintenance of healthy habits to promote overall well-being. For cervical cancer survivors specifically, survivorship involves regular surveillance testing and close monitoring for any symptoms that may indicate a recurrence of the disease. This comprehensive approach ensures that survivors receive ongoing medical attention and support as they transition from active treatment to long-term health management.
Relationships:
  - Source: SURVIVORSHIP
  - Target: CERVICAL CANCER
  - Description: After cervical cancer treatment, patients enter survivorship and undergo surveillance for recurrence.

---</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">3</data>
