    <node id="RISK FACTORS THAT INCREASE SUSCEPTIBILITY INCLUDE IMMUNOSUPPRESSION (SUCH AS FROM HIV/AIDS), SMOKING, HIGH PARITY, ORAL CONTRACEPTIVE USE, EARLY SEXUAL ACTIVITY, MULTIPLE SEXUAL PARTNERS, AND HISTORY OF SEXUALLY TRANSMITTED INFECTIONS. AT THE MOLECULAR LEVEL, DNA MUTATIONS IN CERVICAL CELLS MAKE THEM ABNORMAL, LEADING TO MALIGNANT TRANSFORMATION. THE DISEASE IS STAGED USING THE FIGO SYSTEM, AND TREATMENT IS TAILORED TO THE STAGE AND INDIVIDUAL PATIENT CIRCUMSTANCES [DATA: ENTITIES (585, 918, 921, 916, 927, 928, 915, 959); RELATIONSHIPS (2250, 2252, 2258, 2261); SOURCES (169, 172)].">
