    <node id="RADIATION THERAPY FOR THE EYES">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Radiation therapy for the eyes is a treatment method for primary CNS lymphoma in the eyes. It can be delivered by expanding WBRT to include the eyes or by focusing radiation only on the eyes at a lower dose, and it usually treats both eyes at the same time. Possible side effects include temporary or permanent vision problems and cataracts.
Relationships:
  - Source: RADIATION THERAPY FOR THE EYES
  - Target: PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA IN THE EYES
  - Description: Radiation therapy for the eyes is used to treat primary CNS lymphoma in the eyes</data>
