    <node id="ANAL CANCER FOUNDATION">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">The Anal Cancer Foundation is a dedicated organization focused on the fight against anal cancer. As its name indicates, the foundation concentrates its efforts on this specific disease, providing comprehensive resources and support. It operates a website at analcancerfoundation.org, where individuals can access information and learn more about its initiatives. The foundation is particularly committed to supporting both anal cancer patients and their caregivers. Among its key programs is the Peer-To-Peer Support Program, which connects those affected by the disease with others who share similar experiences. For direct inquiries, the foundation can be reached via email at connect@analcancerfoundation.org. Through its resources, patient and caregiver support, and peer connection program, the Anal Cancer Foundation serves as a vital source of assistance and information for the anal cancer community.
Relationships:
  - Source: ANAL CANCER FOUNDATION
  - Target: NCCN
  - Description: The text lists the NCCN Guidelines and the Anal Cancer Foundation’s Peer-To-Peer Support Program as support resources for cancer survivors
  - Source: NCCN
  - Target: ANAL CANCER FOUNDATION
  - Description: The NCCN Guidelines for Patients list the Anal Cancer Foundation as a resource.
  - Source: ANAL CANCER FOUNDATION
  - Target: THOM
  - Description: Thom is an anal cancer survivor quoted in the same survivorship resource that also presents Anal Cancer Foundation support services
  - Source: ANAL CANCER FOUNDATION
  - Target: PEER-TO-PEER SUPPORT PROGRAM
  - Description: The Anal Cancer Foundation runs the Peer-To-Peer Support Program and provides contact for matching patients/caregivers with peer volunteers. The Anal Cancer Foundation runs and offers the Peer-To-Peer Support Program</data>
