      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Melanoma is a type of cancer that most commonly arises as a skin cancer, though it can also develop in other mucosal surfaces, such as the anus, where it is known as anal melanoma, a rare form of anal cancer. The entity is referenced in text that directs readers to the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, which provide detailed, patient-focused information on this disease. These guidelines are available specifically for melanoma and cover aspects of diagnosis, treatment, and supportive care. In summary, melanoma is a serious cancer, with skin being its primary site, and anal melanoma representing a rare variant; authoritative patient guidance is accessible through the NCCN Guidelines for Patients.
