    <node id="T-ALL">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">T-ALL, the acronym for T-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia, is a subtype of acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) that originates in T-cell lymphocytes. As one of the two main types of ALL, it is less common than B-ALL. This condition may cause an enlarged thymus. Treatment options for T-ALL include participation in a clinical trial or chemotherapy.
