      <data key="d1">B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia (B-ALL) is a subtype of ALL that develops in B-cell lymphocytes. It is more common than T-ALL. When B-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in the lymph nodes instead of the bone marrow, it is called B-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma.
