      <data key="d4">ENTITY: T-CELL LYMPHOBLASTIC LYMPHOMA
Description: T-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma, also known as T-LL or T-LBL, is a condition that occurs when T-cell lymphoblasts—immature cells that normally develop into T lymphocytes—grow primarily in the thymus rather than in the bone marrow. This abnormal growth in the thymus is a defining feature of the disease, distinguishing it from other lymphoblastic malignancies that more commonly arise in the bone marrow.
