    <node id="PSA DENSITY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">PSA density is a calculated clinical value that divides a patient's PSA (prostate-specific antigen) level by prostate size, typically measured via ultrasound or other imaging to determine prostate volume. This measurement accounts for prostate size, providing a more nuanced assessment than PSA level alone. A higher PSA density indicates a greater likelihood of prostate cancer, making it a useful tool for evaluating cancer risk.
Relationships:
  - Source: PROSTATE CANCER
  - Target: PSA DENSITY
  - Description: Higher PSA density indicates a greater likelihood of prostate cancer.
  - Source: PSA DENSITY
  - Target: PROSTATE CANCER
  - Description: A higher PSA density indicates a greater likelihood of prostate cancer
  - Source: PSA LEVEL
  - Target: PSA DENSITY
  - Description: PSA density is calculated by dividing PSA level by prostate size</data>
