    <node id="LYNCH SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Lynch syndrome is an inherited condition caused by mutations in mismatch repair (MMR) genes. It is a hereditary disorder that significantly increases the risk of developing several types of cancer, most notably colon cancer, as well as uterine (endometrial), ovarian, and other cancers. Lynch syndrome can also cause hereditary ovarian cancer and may increase the risk of developing an adrenal tumor. Because of its strong hereditary nature and elevated cancer risks, Lynch syndrome is recognized as a factor that may make germline genetic testing appropriate for affected individuals and their families.

Relationships:
  - Source: GENETIC TESTING
  - Target: LYNCH SYNDROME
  - Description: Genetic testing can identify Lynch syndrome and other hereditary syndromes

---</data>
