    <node id="SOURCE: BIOPSY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Biopsy and biomarker testing are closely related procedures in the diagnosis and treatment of cancer. A biopsy involves obtaining a sample of tumor tissue from the patient. This biopsy sample is then used for biomarker testing, which analyzes the tumor for specific molecular components, such as genes, proteins, or other biomarkers. In other words, biomarker testing relies on a tissue sample obtained through biopsy, allowing healthcare providers to identify molecular characteristics of the tumor that may guide treatment decisions. Together, biopsy and biomarker testing enable a detailed understanding of the tumor's biology.</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">    Target: BIOMARKER TESTING
    Description: Biopsy and biomarker testing are closely related procedures in the diagnosis and treatment of cancer. A biopsy involves obtaining a sample of tumor tissue from the patient. This biopsy sample is then used for biomarker testing, which analyzes the tumor for specific molecular components, such as genes, proteins, or other biomarkers. In other words, biomarker testing relies on a tissue sample obtained through biopsy, allowing healthcare providers to identify molecular characteristics of the tumor that may guide treatment decisions. Together, biopsy and biomarker testing enable a detailed understanding of the tumor's biology.
</data>
    </node>
