    <node id="SOURCE: RECURRENCE">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Biomarker testing plays a critical role in the management of recurrent cancers, helping to guide treatment decisions and identify potential therapeutic options. In the context of recurrent ovarian cancer, biomarker testing is used to help direct treatment by providing information that can inform which therapies are most likely to be effective for the individual patient. For recurrent cervical cancer, biomarker testing is specifically recommended for all patients with disease recurrence, as it serves to identify targeted therapy options or determine eligibility for clinical trials. Thus, across both recurrent ovarian and recurrent cervical cancers, biomarker testing is an essential tool for personalizing care after a recurrence, enabling clinicians to match patients with the most appropriate treatments, including targeted therapies, and to explore clinical trial opportunities when standard options are limited.</data>
