      <data key="d1">Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) is a type of medical imaging test that uses strong magnetic fields and radio waves—without exposing the patient to radiation—to produce detailed pictures of soft tissues in the body. It is particularly useful for examining structures such as the uterus, cervix, and vagina, and can help determine whether cancer has spread to nearby areas.
Relationships: (No explicit relationships listed in the provided data for this entity)</data>
