    <node id="TECHNOLOGIST">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">The imaging technologist, also referred to as a technician, is the person who operates the MRI machine. This individual is responsible for checking for metal in the body and collecting the images produced during the scan. Additionally, the technologist should be informed about any metal present in a patient's body before an MRI is performed, as this is a critical safety measure.
