Description: MAMMOGRAM is an imaging test that produces an x-ray picture of the inside of the breast using low-dose x-rays. It may be performed as a standard 2D digital mammogram or as a 3D mammogram, known as tomosynthesis. The mammogram is used both for breast cancer screening and for the evaluation or diagnosis of breast conditions. It is interpreted by a breast diagnostic radiologist. In addition to screening and diagnosis, a mammogram can also be used to guide a biopsy; when used in this way, the procedure is called a stereotactic needle biopsy.
Relationships: (No explicit relationships listed in the provided data for this entity)</data>
