    <node id="POSITRON EMISSION TOMOGRAPHY (PET)">
      <data key="d3">3</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">POSITRON EMISSION TOMOGRAPHY (PET) is a medical imaging technique that uses a sugar-based radiotracer to detect cancer cells and assess the spread of cancer. It may be performed alone or combined with computed tomography (CT) or magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) for more detailed diagnostic information.
Relationships: (No relationships were provided in the data for this entity.)</data>
