    <node id="BREAST EXAM">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A breast exam is a component of a physical examination that specifically checks the breasts for abnormalities. It is a physical exam that helps find breast cancer at its earliest, most treatable stages. Thus, the breast exam serves both as a general assessment of breast health and as a screening tool for early cancer detection.
Relationships:
  - Source: BREAST CANCER SCREENING
  - Target: BREAST EXAM
  - Description: Breast exams are part of breast cancer screening.
  - Source: BREAST EXAM
  - Target: REGULAR SCREENING
  - Description: Regular screening includes breast exams.
  - Source: BREAST CANCER
  - Target: BREAST EXAM
  - Description: Breast exams help find breast cancer at earlier, more treatable stages.
  - Source: BREAST EXAM
  - Target: EARLY DETECTION
  - Description: Breast exams help achieve early detection of breast cancer.
  - Source: PHYSICAL EXAM
  - Target: BREAST EXAM
  - Description: A physical exam includes a breast exam.
  - Source: CLINICAL STAGING
  - Target: BREAST EXAM
  - Description: The breast exam is part of the physical exam that contributes to clinical staging.</data>
