    <node id="CUTANEOUS SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA OF THE VERMILION LIP">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma of the vermilion lip is a squamous cell carcinoma occurring at the area where the skin and the lip meet on the outside of the mouth. It is not included in the mouth cancer book but is covered in NCCN Guidelines for Patients: Squamous Cell Skin Cancer.
Relationships:
  - Source: MOUTH CANCER
  - Target: CUTANEOUS SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA OF THE VERMILION LIP
  - Description: Cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma of the vermilion lip is explicitly excluded from the mouth cancer book, distinguishing it from cancers of the mucosal lip and oral cavity.</data>
