    <node id="DIRECT LARYNGOSCOPY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Direct laryngoscopy is a detailed diagnostic procedure performed under general anesthesia in an operating room. Using a laryngoscope (a specialized scope) placed in the back of the throat, the doctor is able to examine deeper areas of the throat than is possible with a standard laryngoscopy. This technique allows the physician to visualize the throat thoroughly, take a tissue sample for biopsy, identify the primary tumor, and determine whether the tumor is resectable (surgically removable).
Relationships: None listed in the provided data.</data>
