    </node>
    <node id="COMPUTED TOMOGRAPHY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Computed tomography (CT), also called a CT scan, is a type of imaging test that uses multiple X-rays of the same body part. It is a detailed X-ray imaging procedure that takes numerous pictures from different angles and combines them into three-dimensional (3-D) images. To make certain structures clearer, a contrast agent may be used during the scan.
Relationships:
  - No specific relationships listed in the provided data for this entity.</data>
