    <node id="BREAST CANCER STAGING">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Breast cancer staging is the application of cancer staging to breast cancer, used to reflect prognosis and guide treatment decisions; it is often done before and after surgery.
Relationships:
  - Source: BREAST CANCER STAGING
  - Target: BIOPSY
  - Description: Biopsy samples are tested for ER, PR, HER2, and grade, which are used in breast cancer staging
  - Source: BREAST CANCER STAGING
  - Target: DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM
  - Description: Diagnostic mammograms provide imaging information used in breast cancer staging
  - Source: BREAST CANCER STAGING
  - Target: IMAGING TESTS
  - Description: Imaging tests are used to take pictures of the inside of the body and are used in cancer staging
  - Source: BREAST CANCER STAGING
  - Target: CLINICAL STAGING
  - Description: Breast cancer staging includes clinical staging before treatment
  - Source: BREAST CANCER STAGING
  - Target: SURGERY
  - Description: Surgery provides tissue for pathologic staging, and pathologic staging applies to people who had surgery as initial treatment
  - Source: BREAST CANCER STAGING
  - Target: TREATMENT
  - Description: Breast cancer staging is used to guide treatment decisions and predict prognosis
  - Source: CANCER STAGING
  - Target: BREAST CANCER STAGING
  - Description: Breast cancer staging is the specific application of cancer staging to breast cancer
  - Source: BREAST CANCER STAGING
  - Target: PATHOLOGIC STAGING
  - Description: Breast cancer staging includes pathologic staging after surgery
  - Source: BREAST CANCER STAGING
  - Target: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSY
  - Description: A sentinel lymph node biopsy is used to check lymph node spread, a component of breast cancer staging
  - Source: BREAST CANCER STAGING
  - Target: DRUG THERAPY
  - Description: If drug therapy is given before surgery, the breast cancer stage may be labeled with a ypT prefix</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
