    <node id="LUNG CANCER SCREENING">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Lung cancer screening is a medical screening procedure for people at risk of lung cancer, performed to detect the disease at its earliest and most treatable stage.
Relationships:
  - Source: LUNG CANCER SCREENING
  - Target: CANCER SCREENING
  - Description: Lung cancer screening is a specific type of cancer screening
  - Source: LUNG CANCER SCREENING
  - Target: EARLY DETECTION
  - Description: Lung cancer screening is performed to enable early detection of lung cancer before symptoms begin
  - Source: NCCN
  - Target: LUNG CANCER SCREENING
  - Description: NCCN provides patient guidelines and a cancer app referenced in the lung cancer screening educational material
  - Source: LUNG CANCER SCREENING
  - Target: RISK ASSESSMENT
  - Description: Risk assessment determines whether a patient qualifies for lung cancer screening</data>
