    <node id="DISTRESS SCREENING">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Distress screening is a structured assessment used to identify emotional distress in cancer patients as part of their comprehensive cancer care. It evaluates a patient’s level of mental, physical, social, or spiritual distress, including depression, anxiety, and sleep issues. By systematically assessing these domains, distress screening helps care teams recognize and address the multifaceted challenges that can accompany a cancer diagnosis and treatment.
Relationships:
  - Source: TESTING FOR BREAST CANCER
  - Target: DISTRESS SCREENING
  - Description: Distress screening is part of the testing and care process for breast cancer.</data>
