In the context of rectal cancer, watch and wait is a management option following chemoradiation, in which no immediate additional treatment is given. Instead, the patient is closely monitored for signs of residual or recurrent disease. This strategy may be considered when a complete clinical response is achieved after chemoradiation, thereby avoiding surgery or further immediate therapy.

