    <node id="LOCAL EXCISION">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Local excision is a surgical procedure that removes only the tumor and a small area of surrounding tissue. It is a recommended treatment option for some early-stage, low-risk perianal cancers, particularly slow-growing stage I and II perianal cancers. In certain cases, local excision may be used as an alternative to chemoradiation for some anal cancers. This approach offers a more limited resection than broader surgeries, making it suitable for select patients whose tumors meet specific criteria.
Relationships: None listed in the provided data.</data>
