    <node id="PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Platinum chemotherapy is a type of cancer treatment that uses drugs containing the metal platinum. This category includes well-known agents such as cisplatin and carboplatin. It is commonly administered during radiation therapy, often concurrently with external beam radiation therapy (EBRT) as part of a chemoradiation regimen. This approach is specifically utilized in the treatment of cancers such as squamous cell skin cancer and cervical cancer, among others. As a systemic therapy, platinum chemotherapy works by interfering with DNA replication in rapidly dividing cancer cells, enhancing the effects of radiation when given together.
Relationships:
  - Source: CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Target: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Platinum chemotherapy is a type of chemotherapy that contains platinum drugs such as cisplatin and carboplatin.
  - Source: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Target: CHEMORADIATION
  - Description: Chemoradiation is a cancer treatment modality that combines radiation therapy with platinum chemotherapy. Specifically, chemoradiation consists of external beam radiation therapy (EBRT) delivered alongside platinum-based chemotherapy agents. This approach integrates the radiosensitizing and cytotoxic effects of platinum chemotherapy with the targeted tumor-killing effects of EBRT, allowing for enhanced treatment efficacy. In this context, the platinum chemotherapy is administered concurrently with radiation, and this combination is referred to as chemoradiation. Thus, the entity known as PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY is a key component of CHEMORADIATION, which is defined by the pairing of platinum drugs with external beam radiation.
  - Source: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Target: BRACHYTHERAPY
  - Description: Brachytherapy may be given along with platinum chemotherapy in the treatment of locally advanced cervical cancer
  - Source: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Target: VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY
  - Description: Vaginal brachytherapy may be given in addition to EBRT and platinum chemotherapy
  - Source: EBRT
  - Target: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: EBRT is given together with platinum chemotherapy as part of chemoradiation for cervical cancer
  - Source: EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY (EBRT)
  - Target: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Platinum chemotherapy may be given during the same time period as EBRT
  - Source: VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY
  - Target: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Vaginal brachytherapy may be given in addition to platinum chemotherapy</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">7</data>
