    <node id="PLATINUM-BASED CHEMOTHERAPY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Platinum-based chemotherapy is a specific chemotherapy regimen commonly recommended for use in conjunction with radiation therapy, particularly when systemic therapy is planned as part of the treatment strategy. It is also utilized as a systemic therapy for metastatic cervical cancer, often administered as a combination regimen to enhance therapeutic effectiveness.
Relationships:
  - Source: PLATINUM-BASED CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Target: COMBINATION REGIMEN
  - Description: Platinum-based chemotherapy is often given with one or two other medicines as a combination regimen
  - Source: CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Target: PLATINUM-BASED CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Platinum-based chemotherapy is a specific type of chemotherapy.
  - Source: RADIATION THERAPY
  - Target: PLATINUM-BASED CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Platinum-based chemotherapy is a recommended option for use with radiation.
  - Source: SYSTEMIC THERAPY
  - Target: PLATINUM-BASED CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Systemic therapy is a treatment approach used in cancer care, encompassing a range of drug-based treatments that circulate throughout the body. When systemic therapy is planned, platinum-based chemotherapy is a recommended option. This is particularly relevant in the context of metastatic cervical cancer, where systemic therapy is usually platinum-based chemotherapy. Thus, platinum-based chemotherapy serves as a key component of systemic therapy, especially for patients with metastatic cervical cancer.</data>
