    <edge source="NCCN" target="CHEMOTHERAPY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides supportive-care information and patient guidelines that are directly relevant to individuals undergoing chemotherapy. In its patient education materials, the NCCN describes chemotherapy as a type of systemic therapy, meaning it travels through the bloodstream to treat cancer cells throughout the body. Together, these descriptions highlight the NCCNs dual role in both educating patients about the nature of chemotherapy and offering practical guidance for managing treatment-related care.</data>
      <data key="d8">NCCN</data>
    </edge>
