    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="UNITED STATES" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">NCCN Cancer Centers, associated with the National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN), are located throughout the United States. These centers are listed as a U.S. resource for finding clinical trials, with the NCCN providing a directory of cancer centers within the country. The listings serve as a reference for individuals seeking clinical trial information, highlighting the role of NCCN Cancer Centers in the United States as accessible points for trial discovery. In summary, NCCN Cancer Centers are U.S.-based institutions, identified through the NCCN, and are specifically catalogued as a resource for locating clinical trials in the United States.</data>
      <data key="d8">NCCN</data>
    </edge>
