    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="RICHTER TRANSFORMATION" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The NCCN (National Comprehensive Cancer Network) Guidelines for Patients describe Richter transformation as a possible complication of chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) that can lead to more aggressive lymphomas. Additionally, the NCCN Guidelines for Patients address caring for Richter transformation as part of living with CLL/SLL (chronic lymphocytic leukemia/small lymphocytic lymphoma). Together, these descriptions indicate that Richter transformation is recognized by the NCCN as both a significant CLL complication and an important aspect of ongoing patient care and disease management within the broader context of CLL/SLL.</data>
      <data key="d8">RICHTER TRANSFORMATION</data>
    </edge>
