    </edge>
    <edge source="PROSTATE CANCER" target="PSA DENSITY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Higher PSA density indicates a greater likelihood of prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d8">PROSTATE CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PROSTATE CANCER" target="METASTASIS" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Prostate cancer can advance by metastasis, a process defined as the spread of cancer cells outside the prostate to other organs and tissues. This form of progression is characteristic of advanced-stage prostate cancer. Metastasis occurs when cancer cells travel through the bloodstream or the lymphatic system, enabling the cancer to disseminate beyond the prostate to distant sites in the body. In this way, prostate cancer metastasis involves the movement of malignant cells from the prostate via circulatory or lymphatic routes, ultimately establishing secondary growths in other organs and tissues.</data>
      <data key="d8">PROSTATE CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PROSTATE CANCER" target="UNITED STATES" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text describes U.S. statistics showing that Black males are more likely to develop, be diagnosed at an advanced stage, and die from prostate cancer compared with white males.</data>
      <data key="d8">PROSTATE CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PROSTATE CANCER" target="ADVANCED-STAGE PROSTATE CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Prostate cancer is a disease that can be grouped into categories based on its progression. One such category is advanced-stage prostate cancer. Advanced-stage prostate cancer is a stage of prostate cancer in which the cancer has spread outside the prostate gland. In this context, advanced-stage prostate cancer is defined as a distinct category or stage within the broader classification of prostate cancer, representing the more severe end of the disease spectrum where the malignancy has metastasized beyond the organ of origin.</data>
      <data key="d8">PROSTATE CANCER</data>
    </edge>
