    <edge source="SMOKEFREE.GOV" target="CDC" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">SmokeFree.gov and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) are both recognized as online support resources for individuals seeking to quit tobacco use. Specifically, SmokeFree.gov is listed as an online support option to help people quit smoking or vaping, while the CDCs website, CDC.gov/tobacco, is also listed as an online support resource for quitting tobacco. Together, they serve as accessible digital tools for tobacco cessation, offering guidance and assistance to those looking to stop using tobacco products.</data>
      <data key="d8">CDC</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SMOKEFREE.GOV" target="PATIENT" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">SmokeFree.gov is an online support resource for the patient to quit smoking or vaping</data>
      <data key="d8">PATIENT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BETOBACCOFREE.GOV" target="CDC" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">BeTobaccoFree.gov and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) are both recognized as online support resources for individuals seeking to quit tobacco use. Specifically, the CDC provides these resources through its dedicated website, CDC.gov/tobacco. Together, BeTobaccoFree.gov and the CDC serve as accessible online support options to help people quit smoking or vaping. Both entities are listed as credible sources of assistance for tobacco cessation, offering guidance and resources for those looking to stop using tobacco products.</data>
      <data key="d8">CDC</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CDC.GOV/TOBACCO" target="CDC" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">CDC.gov/tobacco is the official tobacco resource page of the CDC (Centers for Disease Control and Prevention). As a dedicated web resource maintained by the CDC, it is designed to provide reliable information and online support for individuals looking to quit smoking or vaping. The CDC is the organization responsible for and associated with this website, ensuring that the content and resources offered align with public health guidelines and evidence-based cessation strategies.</data>
      <data key="d8">CDC</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DEEP VEIN THROMBOSIS" target="HYSTERECTOMY AND BSO" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Recent abdominal surgery is a risk factor for developing deep vein thrombosis, so surgery patients are monitored for blood clots</data>
      <data key="d8">DEEP VEIN THROMBOSIS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BLOOD THINNERS" target="DEEP VEIN THROMBOSIS" id="0">
