    </edge>
    <edge source="DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM" target="PROSTATE CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A digital rectal exam (DRE) is a clinical procedure used to assess the prostate gland, particularly in the context of prostate cancer. During the exam, a healthcare provider directly checks the prostate for signs of cancer, evaluating its size and texture. The information obtained contributes to the overall assessment of prostate cancer risk and helps guide further diagnostic steps. Thus, the digital rectal exam serves as a key component in the detection and evaluation of prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d8">PROSTATE CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM" target="DIAGNOSTIC TESTING" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">If a digital rectal exam suggests prostate cancer, diagnostic testing may be offered.</data>
      <data key="d8">DIAGNOSTIC TESTING</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM" target="PSA TEST" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A PSA test (prostate-specific antigen test) and a digital rectal exam are two initial screening procedures commonly used together to evaluate prostate health and assess the possible presence of prostate cancer. The PSA test measures the level of prostate-specific antigen in the blood, while the digital rectal exam involves a physical examination of the prostate gland. When used in combination, these tests help healthcare providers determine whether further diagnostic steps, such as a prostate biopsy, are needed. Their combined use provides a more complete evaluation than either test alone, aiding in the early detection and informed decision-making regarding prostate conditions.</data>
      <data key="d8">DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM" target="RECTUM" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Digital rectal exam involves inserting a finger into the rectum.</data>
      <data key="d8">RECTUM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM" target="ANUS" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Digital rectal exam involves inserting a gloved, lubricated finger into the anus.</data>
      <data key="d8">ANUS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM" target="ANOSCOPY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Both DREs and anoscopy are follow-up tests recommended after treatment for cancer in lymph nodes only</data>
      <data key="d8">ANOSCOPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM" target="BIOPSY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A digital rectal exam (DRE) is a clinical procedure used to assess the prostate gland. When an irregular or hardened area is detected during this exam, it serves as a key indicator for further investigation. The results of the digital rectal exam directly inform the clinical decision of whether a prostate biopsy is necessary. Thus, the DRE acts as an initial screening tool, and any suspicious findingssuch as firmness or irregularitiesprompt the consideration of a biopsy to obtain definitive tissue diagnosis.</data>
      <data key="d8">DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM" target="ANAL CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Digital rectal exam is important for diagnosis, staging, and follow-up of anal cancer</data>
      <data key="d8">DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM" target="IMAGING" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A digital rectal exam is used along with imaging and PSA tests to evaluate the prostate</data>
