      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">B-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma occurs when B-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in lymph nodes instead of the bone marrow, a presentation of B-ALL. When B-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in the lymph nodes instead of the bone marrow, B-ALL is called B-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d8">B-CELL ACUTE LYMPHOBLASTIC LEUKEMIA</data>
    </edge>
