      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">T-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma occurs when T-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in the thymus instead of the bone marrow, a presentation of T-ALL. When T-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in the thymus instead of the bone marrow, T-ALL is called T-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d8">T-CELL ACUTE LYMPHOBLASTIC LEUKEMIA</data>
    </edge>
