      <data key="d7">Para-aortic nodes may be removed through lymph node removal.</data>
      <data key="d8">PARA-AORTIC NODES</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MOUTH CANCER" target="CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Mouth cancer is a type of cancer that develops in the oral cavity.</data>
      <data key="d8">MOUTH CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MOUTH CANCER" target="HEAD AND NECK CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Mouth cancer is a type of head and neck cancer. It belongs to the broader category of head and neck cancers, which includes several distinct cancer types. Thus, mouth cancer is one of the several cancers grouped under the head and neck cancer classification.</data>
      <data key="d8">MOUTH CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MOUTH CANCER" target="CANCER TREATMENT" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Cancer treatment for mouth cancer is based on tumor location and cancer stage</data>
      <data key="d8">MOUTH CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MOUTH CANCER" target="SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) is the most common type of mouth cancer. Mouth cancer encompasses various malignancies, and among them, squamous cell carcinoma is the most frequently diagnosed form. Both statements confirm that SCC, also referred to as squamous cell carcinoma, represents the predominant subtype of mouth cancer.</data>
      <data key="d8">MOUTH CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MOUTH CANCER" target="CUTANEOUS SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA OF THE VERMILION LIP" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma of the vermilion lip is explicitly excluded from the mouth cancer book, distinguishing it from cancers of the mucosal lip and oral cavity.</data>
      <data key="d8">MOUTH CANCER</data>
    </edge>
