      <data key="d7">The technologist operates the MRI machine, checks for metal, and collects the images</data>
      <data key="d8">MRI</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLOSED MRI" target="MRI" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Closed MRI is a type of MRI and is noted as more common than open MRI.</data>
      <data key="d8">MRI</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLOSED MRI" target="OPEN MRI" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Closed MRI and open MRI are two types of MRI scanners. Both are alternative designs used for magnetic resonance imaging. Closed MRI is more common than open MRI.</data>
      <data key="d8">OPEN MRI</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLOSED MRI" target="CLAUSTROPHOBIA" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Closed MRI's small, enclosed space can be particularly difficult for patients with claustrophobia</data>
      <data key="d8">CLOSED MRI</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEALTH CARE CENTERS" target="MRI" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Some health care centers offer an open MRI scanner option.</data>
      <data key="d8">MRI</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAMMOGRAM" target="MRI" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Mammograms and MRIs are imaging tests interpreted by a breast diagnostic radiologist</data>
      <data key="d8">MRI</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAMMOGRAM" target="MAMMOGRAM SCREENING" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Mammogram screening is the use of mammograms to screen for breast cancer</data>
      <data key="d8">MAMMOGRAM SCREENING</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAMMOGRAM" target="SCREENING MAMMOGRAM" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A mammogram is a medical imaging procedure used to examine breast tissue. A screening mammogram is a specific type of mammogram that is performed regularly as a routine preventive measure, even when the individual has no symptoms or signs of breast disease. Screening mammograms are conducted on a scheduled basis, typically for early detection of breast abnormalities, including cancer, in asymptomatic individuals.</data>
      <data key="d8">SCREENING MAMMOGRAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAMMOGRAM" target="EARLY DETECTION" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Mammograms are used for early detection of breast cancer</data>
      <data key="d8">MAMMOGRAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAMMOGRAM" target="BIOPSY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Mammogram can be used to guide a biopsy.</data>
