    <edge source="MAMMOGRAM" target="DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A mammogram is an imaging examination used to examine breast tissue. A diagnostic mammogram is a specific type of mammogram performed when there are symptoms or abnormal findings that require further evaluation. Specifically, diagnostic mammograms are used to assess symptoms such as a lump, pain, or nipple discharge, or to follow up on abnormal results from a routine screening mammogram. In essence, while a screening mammogram is used for early detection in asymptomatic individuals, a diagnostic mammogram is a focused examination intended to clarify and evaluate suspicious signs or prior screening abnormalities, providing more detailed imaging to aid in diagnosis.</data>
      <data key="d8">MAMMOGRAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAMMOGRAM" target="ULTRASOUND" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Mammograms and ultrasound are imaging tests used in breast cancer evaluation</data>
      <data key="d8">MAMMOGRAM</data>
    </edge>
