    </edge>
    <edge source="BLADDER REMOVAL SURGERY" target="BCG SHORTAGE" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Bladder removal surgery is an option for high-risk patients if regular BCG treatment is unavailable due to shortage.</data>
      <data key="d8">BLADDER REMOVAL SURGERY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRANSURETHRAL RESECTION OF BLADDER TUMOR (TURBT)" target="RADICAL CYSTECTOMY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Both TURBT and radical cystectomy are surgical treatment options for bladder cancer; TURBT removes tumors from the bladder wall and radical cystectomy removes the bladder.</data>
      <data key="d8">RADICAL CYSTECTOMY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRANSURETHRAL RESECTION OF BLADDER TUMOR (TURBT)" target="BLADDER REMOVAL SURGERY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">TURBT and bladder removal surgery are both surgical procedures used to treat bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d8">BLADDER REMOVAL SURGERY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TURBT" target="CHEMOTHERAPY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Chemotherapy may be given before or after surgery depending on the type or stage of bladder cancer; TURBT is the surgical procedure discussed.</data>
      <data key="d8">TURBT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TURBT" target="INTRAVESICAL BCG THERAPY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Intravesical BCG therapy is scheduled after TURBT and at intervals after the procedure.</data>
      <data key="d8">TURBT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TURBT" target="INTRAVESICAL CHEMOTHERAPY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Intravesical chemotherapy can be given soon after TURBT, within 24 hours of surgery, to clean up remaining cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d8">TURBT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TURBT" target="INTRAVESICAL THERAPY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Intravesical therapy is given after TURBT to destroy any remaining cancer cells and prevent new cancer cell formation.</data>
      <data key="d8">TURBT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADICAL HYSTERECTOMY WITH PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION" target="SURGERY" id="0">
